          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+function"} partial function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⇀
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon A\rightharpoonup B
            between two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            can be turned into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+function"} total function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo ¯
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{f} \colon A\to B_\bot
            by adjoining a further
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/element"} element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and sending all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\in A
            that are not in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            of definition of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            to this new value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot
            \= “undefined” and the rest just to their value under
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_\bot
            corresponds to a unique partial function to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            whence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi B
                    %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_\bot
            is a ‘classifying object’ for these.
          %p
            More generally, a
            %strong partial function classifier
            or
            %strong partial map classifier
            of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representing+object"} representing object
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+maps"} partial maps
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            be a category with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            %strong partial map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⇀
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \rightharpoonup B
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ←
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \leftarrow D \to B
            in which the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\to A
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \hookrightarrow A
            is called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
            of the partial map. Two partial maps are considered
            %em equal
            if they are related by an isomorphism of spans; in this way we obtain a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            of partial maps
            = succeed "." do
