                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Opt_S(q) \to \Omega
              corresponds to giving the domain of definition.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be an object of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}(A, -)
              and the isomorphism to the presheaves these objects represent.
            %p
              An object of the pullback can be described as an arrow
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to S
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \hookrightarrow A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↩
                    %mi B
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookleftarrow B' \to X
              with the property that the induced partial maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↩
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookleftarrow B \to S
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↩
                    %mi B
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookleftarrow B' \to S
              are the same partial map (up to choice of representative for the subobject).
